dzleon@gmail.com wrote:
> Aardvark Joe wrote:
>>pendell@hotmail.com wrote:
>>>The bard songs will be a combination of ring, amulet, scroll, or book
>>>effects.  Some of the effects will be quite positive (remove curse,
>>>scare monster for N turns) others will be negative (destroy armor,
>>>amnesia).

Amnesia?!  Ouch (for a bard)!

>>Besides the comments on the specifics you mentioned, there's
>>one basic problem that I see: when you get down to it, this
>>is really just an alternative to the current spellcasting
>>system.  You learn spells (tunes) from items found in the dungeon,
>>and then cast (play) them using your magic power.  There is the
>>requirement that you have an instrument, but if you start with
>>it then it makes very little difference.  You would have
>>to come up with a method of differentiating it from
>>spellcasting before it would be worth implementing.
> 
> Yes. This class is just a different kind of wizard. personally I think
> that the difference between classes is not what item they use but the
> fact that they make you play the game a little differently. A barbarian
> and a rogue could use the same weapons, but a rogue will be a ranged
> fighter and a barbarian melee, because of the small differences between
> them.

What about the obvious alternative: having special charged instruments 
instead, with some form of recharging over time?  (Not the same as 
existing charged instruments.)  If the bard can only play instruments so 
much, then you don't have the problem of them playing genocide all the 
time.  The mechanic would end up between spells and wands.  You would 
have to experiment with tunes, with some hints when you are partly 
correct, but that would use up the instrument's magical power that could 
otherwise have been used for doing things.  A few "zap self"-type tunes 
(scaled, e.g. half HP lost) would spice up the game a little.

Another random idea: make the player use tunes to specify items, 
monsters, whatever, for tunes that require them to be specified.

> Quest artifact would be something to play against higher-level
> creatures. For pacifying demons, for example. Or maybe it works on all
> creatures but is harder to use. #invoke could tell you tunes for your
> instruments.

An artefact instrument which recharged much quicker would have the same 
effect on Bards as )LoD has on Rangers.  Or it could be a music book, 
which would give you all spells.

